WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.800
Let me set the scene for people.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.570
Please.
Because if nothing else,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.370
I'm a setter of scenes, a scene setter,

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.270
if you will.
(Sona sighs)

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.940
I paint a picture, a mind picture.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.620
We are here at Gourley's lovely home

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.670
and I'm gonna say there's a little bit

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.340
of a Mr. Miyagi in the original
"Karate Kid" vibe here.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.303
Well, that's the nicest thing
anyone's ever said to me.

00:00:19.303 --> 00:00:21.390
No, but like, it's a nice, there's a,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.570
we're in Pasadena and let me just begin

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:28.230
by saying I got in my car to come here

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.770
and I plugged in your address.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.710
And Waze said it was gonna
be an hour and 28 minutes.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.480
Oh.
To get here.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.130
And then Waze started saying

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.460
are you sure you want to go there?

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.950
(Gourley and Sona laughing)

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.200
And I was saying to Waze,

00:00:43.057 --> 00:00:46.920
"Well, he's my friend and
we're doing a podcast."

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.177
And then Waze was like, "Wait a minute,

00:00:49.177 --> 00:00:51.007
isn't your name on the podcast?"

00:00:51.007 --> 00:00:52.290
"Why aren't they doing it at your house?"

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.030
I don't know how Waze
has all this information.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.800
Yeah, I'm not sure I understand that.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.810
Did it take you first
to Santa Monica Airport

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.770
and try to fly you here?

00:00:58.770 --> 00:00:59.970
It took me to Catalina.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:00.979
Yeah.

00:01:00.979 --> 00:01:01.812
(Gourley and Conan chuckling)

00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:02.940
It took me 15 minutes.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.440
Yes, well, that's the thing is--

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.600
It was nice for me.
First of all,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.850
I applaud both of you

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.070
because you've made a very bold choice

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.228
to raise your children in another country.

00:01:13.228 --> 00:01:15.900
(Gourley and Sona laughing)

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.250
I don't know where we are
but I'm not sure we're

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.300
in the United States anymore.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.100
It took me a long, long time to get here.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.270
Come on.
No, look,

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.100
I know people accuse someone like me

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.400
of being in some sort of entitled bubble.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.260
Yeah.
[Gourley] Yeah.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.790
And I have looked into,

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.010
to be fair, having a
bubble built around me.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:32.843
A literal bubble?

00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:34.770
(Gourley and Sona laughing)

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.570
There's, I guess there's a zoning issue.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.880
But I wanted, I wanted an
actual bubble until people--

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.411
You went to the permitting office?

00:01:40.411 --> 00:01:41.244
I went to the permitting office

00:01:41.244 --> 00:01:42.607
and they said, "Sir what you're talking

00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:45.120
about is a big bubble that surrounds you."

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.007
And I said, "Yes, I don't
care what it costs."

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.797
"I have the money, I just
wanna live inside a bubble."

00:01:50.797 --> 00:01:53.197
"And I have this company
that's gonna build it

00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:54.701
for me called Entitle Co."

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.377
(Sona laughing)
And then someone said,

00:01:56.377 --> 00:01:57.240
"It's gonna look bad."

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.202
I didn't understand why.

00:01:59.202 --> 00:02:01.530
But anyway, it was, but once you get here

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.030
and I do say once you get here

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.190
and you've changed your currency

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.230
and had all the requisite
shots, it is lovely.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.460
This is beautiful.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.330
It's beautiful.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.970
You know what, it took me
no time at all to get here.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.210
I came earlier with my boys
to play with your daughter.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.470
Yeah.
Then I went home

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.870
and then I came back,
probably all in the time

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:19.920
that it took you to get here.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.440
But it was really nice
and convenient, and easy.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.740
I had several children
on the way over here.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.573
(Sona laughing)

00:02:25.573 --> 00:02:26.523
Two of them, you know,

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:31.110
it's like transatlantic
travel in the 1780s.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.640
One of them didn't make it.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.442
He got the seagull sickness.

00:02:34.442 --> 00:02:35.871
(Sona laughing)

00:02:35.871 --> 00:02:37.041
(Gourley chuckling)

00:02:37.041 --> 00:02:39.480
But no, it's really nice because again,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.610
I will paint the picture,
we're in a lovely backyard.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.830
And Gourley, I know this about you,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.880
you have excellent taste.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.860
You have very good, he's
got very good taste.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:47.970
He does.
And he's very handy.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.910
And he's built this wonderful oasis.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:53.010
And we're sitting in the backyard.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:57.273
We've got this lovely
Solo Stove in front of us.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.490
That's burning Juniper wood.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.450
Can you smell that?

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.383
It smells really good.

00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:02.216
[Gourley] Oh, it smells so good.

00:03:02.216 --> 00:03:03.990
And I will say, I know there are people

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:04.867
that are like, "Why is Conan

00:03:04.867 --> 00:03:06.600
just mentioning Solo Stove?"

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.580
Solo Stove, maybe we're doing business

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.630
with them, maybe we aren't.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.680
That's not the important thing.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:11.640
We are.
That's a great--

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.770
Yeah, there's Solo Stoves everywhere.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.750
I feel like they sent you like, four?

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.430
They sent five and they sent

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.616
mm, a small forest worth of wood.

00:03:20.616 --> 00:03:21.810
(Sona laughing)
Yeah.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:25.950
The Solo Stove though, is
burning very efficiently

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.750
and wonderfully in front of us.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.750
And I only mention it not
because they are a sponsor.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.174
That's not, but I do love a fire.

00:03:35.174 --> 00:03:37.020
Oh, it's the best.
I love a fire.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.810
And I know that if I was in some sort

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.600
of industrial accident,
if my arm caught fire,

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.650
if people tried to put it out,

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.151
I'd say, "Let's just watch it for a bit."

00:03:45.151 --> 00:03:45.984
(Gourley laughing)

00:03:45.984 --> 00:03:47.430
That's how much I love a fire.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.360
I thoroughly enjoy
sitting around a campfire

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.240
and I can't wait to use this.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.230
They gave me one.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.430
[Sona] Yeah.
I'll just say it.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.100
And the only problem is
if I get this bubble built

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.770
around my house, the
smoke's gonna collect.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.390
Luckily, there's not much smoke.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.610
Well, that's, Sona,
funny you bring that up,

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:08.070
but it's true, there's
not much, not much smoke

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.020
when you get a, it's ingenious.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.550
But listen, maybe Solo Stove

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.110
will come up later, maybe they won't.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:14.100
Who knows?
Right.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.390
It's one of the great mysteries

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.840
of this wonderful outdoor
adventure we're having.

